    "lawCode": "Amd §370, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5329A\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to increasing insurance limits for certain for-hire vehicles\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo clarify that the $1.5 million combined single limit insurance\nrequirement for for-hire vehicles shall include coverage for injury to\nor destruction of property.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one would amend paragraphs (a) and (b) of subdivision (1) of\nsection 370 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law to provide that the \"combined\nsingle limit\" of $1 5 million which is required for for-hire vehicles\nwith a passenger capacity of eight or more persons shall include liabil-\nity coverage for injury to or destruction of property, in addition to\ncoverage for bodily injury or death.\n\nSection two would provide that the bill would become effective simul-\ntaneously with section 13 of Part III of Chapter 59 of the Laws of 2019.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSection 370 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law requires minimum liability\ncoverages for for-hire vehicles based on carrying capacity. Part III of\nChapter 59 of the Laws of 2019 required for-hire vehicles with a capaci-\nty of eight or more persons to carry a minimum of $1.5 million of\nliability coverage in a \"single combined limit.\" This limit included\ncoverage for bodily injury or death. This bill would clarify that mini-\nmum liability coverage of $10,000 per accident for injury to or\ndestruction of property, shall be included within the $1.5 million\nsingle combined limit, rather than an additional coverage.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\nsection 13 of part III of chapter 59 of the laws of 2019, takes effect.\n",
